 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "N_SRC": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 52411,
   "description": "ISRM source cells (first-52411 coarse subset of the InMAP grid)."
  },
  "N_RCV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 52411,
   "description": "ISRM receptor cells (== the source grid, same ordered cell set)."
  },
  "N_ALL": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 596444,
   "description": "Every cell of the full InMAP grid: 8 ground layers of N_SRC cells plus 19 coarse layers of 9324, laid out layer-major. The length of W/S/E/N/TotalPop/MortalityRate and of the eight meteorology arrays (the zarr's `allcells` dimension)."
  },
  "N_LAYER": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 3,
   "description": "SR emission layers. All three are used: plume rise splits every emission record across them with the weights w_sr0/w_sr1/w_sr2, and the sibling loaders ISRM_SR_L0/L1/L2 fix this axis to 0, 1 and 2. The MODEL layers these three were computed for are [0, SR_MODEL_L1, SR_MODEL_L2] = [0, 3, 6] — see SR_MODEL_L1."
  },
  "SR_MODEL_L1": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 3,
   "description": "The MODEL layer SR emission layer 1 was computed for. The SR matrix's `layers` variable — the MODEL layer indices the SR calculation was performed for — is [0, 3, 6] in the authoritative isrm_v1.2.1.ncf on Zenodo. The isrm_v1.2.1.zarr this document reads served [0, 1, 2] instead — a machine-generated arange that displaced the real array during the zarr conversion — UNTIL 2026-08-20, when the store was repaired in place and now serves [0, 3, 6] (root attribute store_version = 1.2.1+repair1). Corroboration independent of the NetCDF: sr/sr.go attaches `description: \"Layer indices for which the SR calculation was performed\"` to `layers`, and the zarr's copy has NO attributes at all while neighbouring InMAP variables (LayerHeight, Dz) keep theirs; the same conversion pass lost the per-cell `Layer` variable and stripped .zattrs off the SR arrays, which is why the shims needed seed_empty_zattrs (the repair restored those too). Zenodo calls the three heights \"ground-level, low-stack, and high-stack\", which [0,3,6] (0-58 m / 253-391 m / 786-1049 m) is and [0,1,2] (three adjacent layers all under 245 m) is not. The matrix DATA is fine — Zenodo's zip is md5-identical across depositions and its rows are byte-identical to the zarr's. So [0,3,6] is DECLARED HERE and is still deliberately NOT read from the store. The repair means the store would now give the right answer, but a declared constant cannot silently change under a document that was validated against it, and the whole reason this value is written down is that reading it once produced a wrong answer nobody could see. Reading it back is a change to make deliberately, with a re-run, not by default. Used here as the layer-major offset SR_MODEL_L1*N_SRC + c into the 596444-cell meteorology arrays."
  },
  "SR_MODEL_L2": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 6,
   "description": "The MODEL layer SR emission layer 2 was computed for — the top entry of `layers`. See SR_MODEL_L1 for the provenance of [0, 3, 6]. Two things ride on this number: it is the upper interpolation node for a plume between SR layers 1 and 2, and it is where `plume_model_layer` saturates, which is what folds InMAP's AboveTopErr case (model layer > 6 -> SR layer 2, weight 1) into the same branch as an exact match."
  },
  "N_REC": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 0,
   "description": "EGU FF10 point-source record count (runtime-discovered; G6)."
  },
  "N_EVERT": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 1,
   "description": "Vertices per emission record: 1, because a point is one vertex. The reader's `nvert_max`."
  },
  "N_XY": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 2,
   "description": "Components of a coordinate: longitude at position 1, latitude at position 2. The xy axis of the reader's `geometry`."
  }
 },
